  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Raising Awareness and Combating Trafficking in Human Organs and Body Parts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the previous year Project (MOZ337) carried out by CEMIRDE about a first Study on Trafficking in Human Organs and Body Parts funded by CAFOD and developed together with &quot;Eduardo Mondalane University of Maputo&quot;; CEMIRDE is going to develop a second phase focusing mainly on activities aimed at raising awareness in local communities and international stakeholders, both inside and outside the Church.
Moreover the awareness raised should translate into concrete behaviours to fight human organs trafficking, whose victims are mainly children.</narrative>
  </description>
